ld advanced="true" description="Destination" name="destination" readonly="true" type="I"><selectionValues><option description="Web">0</option><option description="Desktop">1</option></selectionValues><help>The field defines the dashboard destination: Web or Desktop.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Type" name="type" type="I"><selectionValues><option description="Relative">0</option><option description="Absolute">1</option><option description="Class Instance">2</option></selectionValues><help>The field defines the dashboard type: Absolute or Relative.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Printable" name="printable" type="B"><help>Dashboard type for creating printable reports</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Validity Expression" editor="expression" name="validityExpression" type="S"><editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions><help>The field includes the expression defining context(s) to which the dashboard can be attached.</help><group>Validity</group><defaultValue/></field><field description="Validity Update Rules" name="validityListeners" type="T"><help>This field defines a list of context masks and event names. If the event specified in the Event field occurs in any of contexts matching the mask specified by the Mask field in the same record, the Validity Expression will be recalculated for this context. This allows to make the dashboard valid/invalid for a certain context if some changes occur in it.</help><group>Validity</group><defaultValue><table><format><fields><field description="Context Mask" editor="contextmask" icon="fi_context" keyfield="true" name="mask" type="S"><help>Mask of contexts to monitor events in</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Event" extendableSelectionValues="true" icon="fi_event" keyfield="true" name="event" type="S"><help>Name of Event to listen for</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Target Expression" editor="expression" icon="fi_expression" name="expression" nullable="true" type="S"><editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions><help>If specified, points to a context those validity should be checked. If Target Expression is not specified (what is suitable in most cases), the system checks validity of context in that Event has occurred.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field></fields><bindings><binding><reference>event#choices</reference><expression>{utilities:eventsByMask('{mask}')}</expression></binding></bindings><validators contentType="base64">HEseHQ==</validators></format></table></defaultValue></field><field advanced="true" description="Generate Attached and Detached Events" name="generateAttachedEvents" type="B"><help>Attached and Detached events to be generated after attaching to a context</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Allow Validity For Remote Contexts" name="allowValidityForRemoteContexts" type="B"><help>If enabled then this context will be allowed to attach to remote contexts, connected via distributed architecture</help><group>Validity</group><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Default Context" editor="context" name="defaultContext" nullable="true" type="S"><group>Validity</group><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Closable" name="closable" type="B"><help>This flag defines whether the dashboard can be closed. Non-closable dashboards often play a role of main dashboards in operator UIs.</help><group>Additional Properties</group><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Close Dashboard On Reopen" name="closeDashboardOnReopen" type="B"><group>Additional Properties</group><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Launch as Default Action" name="launchAsDefault" type="B"><help>Defines whether the relative dashboard will open as the default action of contexts it's attached to.</help><group>Additional Properties</group><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Layout Control Panel" name="layoutControlPanel" type="B"><help>This flag defines the visibility of the bottom panel (Save/Load layout and other buttons).</help><group>Additional Properties</group><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Template Processing Expression" editor="expression" name="templateProcessingExpression" nullable="true" type="S"><editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions><help>If specified, it processes the template during dashboard opening and return the modified template</help><group>Additional Properties</group><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Template" editor="context" name="template" nullable="true" type="S"><editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions><help>Dashboard context to be used as template</help><group>Additional Properties</group><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Storage Context" editor="context" name="storageContext" type="S"><defaultValue/></field><field description="Table" name="storageClass" type="S"><defaultValue/></field><field hidden="true" name="resourceBundle" nullable="true" readonly="true" type="S"><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field advanced="true" description="Enable Caching" name="cacheEnabled" type="B"><help>Enables caching of this dashboard for better performance. Once a hidden and cached dashboard is displayed again, its startup bindings are not re-evaluated. Cached dashboards also keep user input (e.g. values in text fields) that were not yet transferred to server's unified data model. This option will only have effect if caching is enabled in Web UI plugin global configuration.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field advanced="true" description="Header Expression" editor="expression" name="headerExpression" nullable="true" type="S"><editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions><help>This expression is evaluated during dashboar