e settings define which data to show and how to present it. The list of settings depends on the element type.</help><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field></fields><bindings><binding><reference>parameters</reference><expression>{.:elementParameters('{type}', '{parameters}')}</expression></binding></bindings><validators contentType="base64">HEseHQ==</validators></format></entry><entry><int>2</int><format maxRecords="1" minRecords="1"><fields><field description="Name" name="name" nullable="true" type="S"><validators contentType="base64">HFIeXHcrXl5OYW1lIG1heSBjb250YWluIG9ubHkgTGF0aW4gbGV0dGVycywgZGlnaXRzLCBhbmQgdW5kZXJzY29yZXMd</validators><help>Unique name of the UI component within the dashboard. Since all UI components are represented by contexts located in the two-level component context tree, a component's name also equals to both the name and full path of the component context.</help><defaultValue>STUB</defaultValue></field><field description="Content Overflow" name="overflow" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Auto">auto</option><option description="Hidden">hidden</option><option description="Scroll">scroll</option><option description="Unset">unset</option><option description="Visible">visible</option></selectionValues><help>&lt;p>Behavior of the content if it overflows the container:&lt;/p>&lt;ul>&lt;li>&lt;b>Auto&lt;/b> — scrollbar will be enabled automatically once the content overflows the container&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Hidden&lt;/b> — all overflowed content will be hidden&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Scroll&lt;/b> — scrollbar is always enabled even if content doesn't overflow the container&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Unset&lt;/b> — cancels inheritance of this property from any sources (e.g. dashboard Style property)&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Visible&lt;/b> — the content will always be visible even it overflows the container&lt;/li>&lt;/ul></help><defaultValue>auto</defaultValue></field><field description="Visible" name="visible" type="B"><help>Controls whether the component is displayed.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Variables Storage" name="variablesStorage" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Breakpoint Data" name="gridBreakpoints" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Context Menu" name="contextMenu" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Show Header" name="showHeader" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window header should be displayed.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Header Title" name="dockTitle" type="S"><help>Dockable window header text.</help><aliases><alias>description</alias></aliases><defaultValue/></field><field description="Header Icon" name="dockIcon" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Maximizable" name="maximizable" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window can be maximized.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Collapsible" name="collapsible" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window can be collapsed.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Movable" name="dockMovable" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window can be moved.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Collapsed" name="dockCollapsed" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window is collapsed.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Floatable" name="dockFloatable" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window can be floated.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Resizable" name="dockResizable" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window can be resized.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Tab Position" name="dockTabPosition" type="S"><sel