ing elements).</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="W" name="w" nullable="true" type="I"><help>Width of the element (for floating elements).</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Dock Location Parent ID" name="dockLocationParentId" type="S"><defaultValue/></field><field description="Dock Location Tab Index" name="dockLocationTabIndex" type="I"><help>If this element was previously docked as a tab, this is its index within the parent tab container before it became a floating element.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Dock Location Panel Index" name="dockLocationPanelIndex" type="I"><help>If this element was previously docked as a panel, this is its index within the parent panel container before it became a floating element.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field></fields></format></entry><entry><int>26</int><format minRecords="1"><fields><field description="Name" name="name" type="S"><validators contentType="base64">HEweMSAyMTQ3NDgzNjQ3HQ==</validators><help>Name of the breakpoint which is the breakpoint's unique ID that is later selected via Current Breakpoint property.</help><defaultValue>none</defaultValue></field><field description="Description" name="description" type="S"><help>Human-readable description of the breakpoint. It's used to select the breakpoint in the Web UI Builder's top toolbar during the editing process.</help><defaultValue>None</defaultValue></field><field description="Value" extendableSelectionValues="true" name="value" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Mobile">320</option><option description="Tablet">800</option><option description="Laptop">1366</option><option description="Full HD">1920</option><option description="QHD">2560</option><option description="Ultra HD">3840</option><option description="None">0</option></selectionValues><help>Maximum screen width in pixels at that the breakpoint is applied. There are some predefi