 rather than record numbers.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Selection Values" name="selvals" type="T"><help>List of values that can be selected for the field via a drop-down menu. A description must be defined for each value. Descriptions are shown when displaying the table to a user, and the values are available when the cell is referenced inside the platform.</help><defaultValue><table><format reorderable="true"><fields><field description="Value" keyfield="true" name="value" nullable="true" type="S"><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Description" name="description" type="S"><defaultValue/></field></fields><validators contentType="base64">HEseHQ==</validators></format></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Extendable Selection Values" name="extselvals" type="B"><help>Flag indicating the field may be set to any value, including ones not listed in Selection Values.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field advanced="true" description="Hidden" name="hidden" type="B"><help>The setting hides the field in the UI, but it remains accessible at the data model level.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field advanced="true" description="Inline" name="inline" type="B"><help>&lt;p>This flag has special meaning for different fields:&lt;/p>&lt;ul>&lt;li>If the Inline flag is set for a Data Block field, the field value will be stored in a dedicated database table. The value will not be initially loaded if the table itself is loaded from the database and sent to a IoT Platform Client or external application. The Data Block value will, however, contain a data block ID that can be used to force loading the Data Block data from the server database. This is suitable for large binary values, such as image, sound, and video files.&lt;/li>&lt;li>If Inline flag is set for a Color field, field value will be used to highlight records of the table when its being viewed/edited in a Data Table Editor. Its often feasible to combine Inline flag with a Hidden flag to hide the Color field itself from the table. See the Row Coloring section below for more information.&lt;/li>&lt;li>If Inline flag is set for a Data Table field, default value of the field will have same format as format of the table to which the field belongs. This effectively enables creation of tables with unlimited nesting using Data Table Editor.&lt;/li>&lt;/ul></help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field advanced="true" description="Encrypted" name="encrypted" type="B"><help>Enables database-level field value encryption.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Help" editor="textarea" name="help" nullable="true" type="S"><validators contentType="base64">HFIeW15ccHtDbnRybH1dKl5eRGVzY3JpcHRpb24gbWF5IGNvbnRhaW4gb25seSBwcmludGFibGUgY2hhcmFjdGVycx0=</validators><help>Contents of the pop-up which is displayed to the user when hovering over a field.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Editor/Viewer" extendableSelectionValues="true" name="editor" nullable="true" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Default"><nullValue/></option><option description="List">list</option><option description="Date">date</option><option description="Time">time</option><option description="Date/Time">dateTime</option><option description="Bar">bar</option><option description="Bytes">bytes</option><option description="Format Mask">formatString</option><option description="Class Instance">instance</option><option description="Time Period">period</option><option description="Foreign Class Instance">foreignInstance</option><option description="Expression">expression</option><option description="Function Selector">functionselector</option><option description="Password">password</option><option description="Text Editor">text</option><option description="HTML">html</option><option description="Text Area">textarea</option><option description="Hierarchical List">hierarchicalList</option><option description="Embedded Text Area">etextarea</option><option description="Context">context</option><option description="Context Mask">contextmask</option><option description="Font">font</option><option description="IP Address">ip</option><option description="Box">box</option><option description="Image">image</option><option description="Sound">sound</option><option description="Hex">hex</option><option description="Reference">reference</option><option description="Activator">activator</option><option description="Code Editor">code</option><option description="Spinner">spinner</option><option description="Event Level">eventLevel</option><option description="Date Range">dateRange</option><option description="Evaluation">evaluation</option></selectionValues><help>This parameter defines how the field is shown and modified in the user interface.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Editor Options" name="editorOptions" nullable="true" type="T"><help>Editor/renderer options that allow fine-tuning rendering of field values in the UI.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Validators" name="validators" nullable="true" type="T"><help>List of validators used to check if value is suitable for the field, as well as validator options. The platform features several pre-configured validators, internally used by the system to verify user input.</help><defaultValue><table><format reorderable="true"><fields><field description="Type" name="validator" nullable="true" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Default"><nullValue/></option><option description="ID">I</option><option description="Limits">L</option><option description="Non-Null">N</option><option description="Regex">R</option><option description="Expression">E</option></selectionValues><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Options" name="options" type="S"><defaultValue/></field></fields><bindings><binding><reference>options#options</reference><expression>{validator} == 'E' ? expressionEditorOptions(null) : ""</expression></binding></bindings></format></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Group" name="group" nullable="true" type="S"><help>A human-readable name of a field group. All fields that belong to the same group will appear together within the UI.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field></fields><bindings><binding><reference>editorOptions</reference><expression>callFunction("utilities", "editorOptions", {type}, {editor}, {editorOptions})</expression></binding><binding><reference>editor#choices</reference><expression>{utilities:editors('{type}')}</expression></binding></bindings><validators contentType="base64">HEseHRxWHh0=</validators></format></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Reorderable" name="reorderable" type="B"><help>This flag indicates that records in this table may be swapped (re-ordered) during table processing.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Unresizable" name="unresizable" type="B"><help>This flag indicates that users cannot add or remove rows when editing the table.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Bindings" name="bindings" type="T"><help>A list of data bindings that define how the values in the table are changed when other table cells, or environment variables, are changed during table processing.</help><defaultValue><table><format reorderable="true"><fields><field description="Target" name="target" type="S"><validators contentType="base64">HEweMSAyMTQ3NDgzNjQ3HQ==</validators><help>The binding's &lt;i>Target&lt;/i> field has the following syntax: &lt;b>variable$field[row]#property&lt;/b>. All elements of the binding target are optional, except for the &lt;b>field&lt;/b>. It indicates the field in the table to which changes should be applied.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Expression" editor="expression" name="expression" type="S"><editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions><validators contentType="base64">HEweMSAyMTQ3NDgzNjQ3HQ==</validators><help>The binding expression may contain only standard references. If a reference points to a cell within the table being edited, it will resolve to the value currently contained in the cell (which may be edited by a user, or written by other binding). In all other cases value will be retrieved from the server context, as described in standard references section.</help><defaultValue/></field></fields></format></table></defaultValue></field><field advanced="true" description="Encoded" editor="textarea" name="encoded" readonly="true" type="S"><help>Encoded table format</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Naming Expression" editor="expression" name="namingExpression" nullable="true" type="S"><editorOptions contentType="base64"></editorOptions><help>An Expression that defines how the table is presented to the users in the interface. It must return a string that will be user as the table's description.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field></fields><validators contentType="base64">HEUeZTIxcGJsSmxZMjl5WkhOOUlEdzlJSHR0WVhoU1pXTnZjbVJ6ZlNBL0lHNTFiR3dnT2lBblZHaGxJRzFoZUdsdGRXMGdiblZ0WW1WeUlHOW1JSEpsWTI5eVpITWdZMkZ1Ym05MElHSmxJR3h2ZDJWeUlIUm9ZVzRnZEdobElHMXBibWx0ZFcwbh0=</validators></format><records><record/></records></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Description" name="description" type="S"><validators contentType="base64">HEweMCAxMDAdHFIeW15ccHtDbnRybH1dKl5eRGVzY3JpcHRpb24gbWF5IGNvbnRhaW4gb25seSBwcmludGFibGUgY2hhcmFjdGVycx0=</validators><help>Format of the custom property.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Help" name="help" nullable="true" type="S"><help>Detailed description of the custom property.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field></fields></format></entry><entry><int>28</int><format maxRecords="1" minRecords="1"><fields><field description="Paper Size" name="pageFormat" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="A0">A0</option><option description="A1">A1</option><option description="A2">A2</option><option description="A3">A3</option><option description="A4">A4</option><option description="A5">A5</option><option description="A6">A6</option><option description="B4">B4</option><option description="B5">B5</option><option description="Letter">Letter</option><option description="Legal">Legal</option><option description="Tabloid">Tabloid</option><option description="Custom">Custom</option></selectionValues><help>Paper size to use for printing. The Page Width and Page Height values are automatically updated based on the selected format.</help><defaultValue>A4</defaultValue></field><field description="Page Orientation" name="orientation" type="I"><selectionValues><option description="Portrait">0</option><option description="Landscape">1</option></selectionValues><help>Page orientation: Portrait (vertical) or Landscape (horizontal).</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Page Width" name="pageWidth" type="I"><help>Page width in pixels. Automatically calculated from the selected Paper Size; set manually when Custom paper size is selected.</help><defaultValue>595</defaultValue></field><field description="Page Height" name="pageHeight" type="I"><help>Page height in pixels. Automatically calculated from the selected Paper Size; set manually when Custom paper size is selected.</help><defaultValue>841</defaultValue></field><field description="Print Page Scale" name="scaleMode" type="I"><selectionValues><option description="Normal">0</option><option description="Fit To Width">1</option><option description="Fit To Height">2</option><option description="Fit To Page">3</option><option description="Custom Number">4</option></selectionValues><help>Scaling mode applied to the dashboard when printing: Normal (no scaling), Fit to Width, Fit to Height, Fit to Page, or Custom Number (use Scale Percent to specify the exact percentage).</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Scale Percent" name="scalePercent" type="I"><help>Scale percentage applied when the Custom Number scaling mode is selected.</help><defaultValue>100</defaultValue></field><field description="Left Margin" name="marginLeft" type="I"><help>Left page margin in pixels.</help><defaultValue>56</defaultValue></field><field description="Right Margin" name="marginRight" type="I"><help>Right page margin in pixels.</help><defaultValue>56</defaultValue></field><field description="Top Margin" name="marginTop" type="I"><help>Top page margin in pixels.</help><defaultValue>56</defaultValue></field><field description="Bottom Margin" name="marginBottom" type="I"><help>Bottom page margin in pixels.</help><defaultValue>56</defaultValue></field><field description="Dataset" name="dataset" nullable="true" type="T"><help>DataTable assigned to the printable dashboard. Components inside band bindings can reference columns by short name: &lt;code>{columnName}&lt;/code> resolves to the dataset column at the current row (row 0 for Summary and other no-row contexts; the per-row index for Detail clones). Use &lt;code>{columnName[N]}&lt;/code> to read an explicit row.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Summary On New Page" name="summaryNewPage" type="B"><help>If enabled, the Summary band always starts on a new page after Detail content. Default: disabled — Summary may share the last Detail page when it fits.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Summary With Page Header/Footer" name="summaryWithPageHeaderFooter" type="B"><help>If enabled, dedicated Summary pages repeat the Page Header and Page Footer bands. Default: disabled — dedicated Summary pages contain only the Summary band itself.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field></fields><bindings><binding><reference>pageWidth</reference><expression>cell({.:pageSizesFromFormat({pageFormat})}, 'pageWidth')</expression></binding><binding><reference>pageHeight</reference><expression>cell({.:pageSizesFromFormat({pageFormat})}, 'pageHeight')</expression></binding><binding><reference>scalePercent#hidden</reference><expression>{scaleMode} != 4</expression></binding></bindings></format></entry><entry><int>29</int><format maxRecords="1" minRecords="1"><fields><field description="Nested Records Settings" name="treeRecordsSettings" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Record Expansion Depth" name="expansionDepth" type="I"><help>Allows nested records to be automatically expanded to the indicated depth. Setting Record Expansion Depth to 1 will automatically open all child nodes of the top-level records, setting it to 2 will open all the children’s child nodes, and so on.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Expanded Records ID" name="expandedRecordsId" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Unique Record-Level Columns" name="uniqueRecordLevelColumns" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Opened Switcher Image" name="openedSwitcherImage" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Closed Switcher Image" name="closedSwitcherImage" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Name" name="name" nullable="true" type="S"><validators contentType="base64">HFIeXHcrXl5OYW1lIG1heSBjb250YWluIG9ubHkgTGF0aW4gbGV0dGVycywgZGlnaXRzLCBhbmQgdW5kZXJzY29yZXMd</validators><help>Unique name of the UI component within the dashboard. Since all UI components are represented by contexts located in the two-level component context tree, a component's name also equals to both the name and full path of the component context.</help><defaultValue>STUB</defaultValue></field><field description="Content Overflow" name="overflow" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Auto">auto</option><option description="Hidden">hidden</option><option description="Scroll">scroll</option><option description="Unset">unset</option><option description="Visible">visible</option></selectionValues><help>&lt;p>Behavior of the content if it overflows the container:&lt;/p>&lt;ul>&lt;li>&lt;b>Auto&lt;/b> — scrollbar will be enabled automatically once the content overflows the container&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Hidden&lt;/b> — all overflowed content will be hidden&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Scroll&lt;/b> — scrollbar is always enabled even if content doesn't overflow the container&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Unset&lt;/b> — cancels inheritance of this property from any sources (e.g. dashboard Style property)&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Visible&lt;/b> — the content will always be visible even it overflows the container&lt;/li>&lt;/ul></help><defaultValue>auto</defaultValue></field><field description="Visible" name="visible" type="B"><help>Controls whether the component is displayed.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Variables Storage" name="variablesStorage" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Breakpoint Data" name="gridBreakpoints" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Context Menu" name="contextMenu" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Show Header" name="showHeader" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window header should be displayed.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Header Title" name="dockTitle" type="S"><help>Dockable window header text.</help><aliases><alias>description</alias></aliases><defaultValue/></field><field description="Header Icon" name="dockIcon" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Maximizable" name="maximizable" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window can be maximized.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Collapsible" name="collapsible" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window can be collapsed.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Movable" name="dockMovable" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window can be moved.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Collapsed" name="dockCollapsed" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window is collapsed.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Floatable" name="dockFloatable" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window can be floated.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Resizable" name="dockResizable" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window can be resized.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Tab Position" name="dockTabPosition" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Top">top</option><option description="Bottom">bottom</option><option description="Left">left</option><option description="Right">right</option></selectionValues><help>Configures the position of tabs appearing when the dockable window is stacked into a tabbed panel with other windows.</help><defaultValue>top</defaultValue></field><field description="Preferred Width" name="dockPreferredWidth" type="I"><help>Desired width of the dockable window when split into another component or a dashboard.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Preferred Height" name="dockPreferredHeight" type="I"><help>Desired height of the dockable window when split into another component or a dashboard.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Minimum Width" name="dockMinimumWidth" type="I"><help>Minimum width of the dockable window when split into another component or a dashboard. Overridden when the viewscreen does not have sufficient space for the minimum width.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Minimum Height" name="dockMinimumHeight" type="I"><help>Minimum height of the dockable window when split into another component or a dashboard. Overridden when the viewscreen does not have sufficient space for the minimum height.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Tab ID" name="tabId" type="S"><help>Dockable tab identifier, which by default is the dockable component name.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Panel ID" name="panelId" type="S"><help>Identified of the panel the dockable component is located in.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Order ID" name="orderId" type="I"><help>Index of tab the dockable component will occupy in a tabbed panel. Indexed from zero, where 0 is the first tab, 1 is the second tab, and so on.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Active Tab" name="dockActive" type="B"><help>Indicates that the dockable component is the selected tab, when that the component is in a tabbed panel.</help><aliases><alias>active</alias></aliases><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Horizontal Position" name="gridx" type="I"><help>In a grid layout, a grid column the component is located in. In an absolute layout, horizontal (X) coordinate of the component in pixels.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Vertical Position" name="gridy" type="I"><help>In a grid layout, a grid row the component is located in. In an absolute layout, vertical (Y) coordinate of the component in pixels.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Width" name="gridWidth" type="I"><validators contentType="base64">HEweMSAyMTQ3NDgzNjQ3HQ==</validators><help>In a grid layout, a number of grid columns the component spans for. In an absolute layout, the width of the component in pixels.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Height" name="gridHeight" type="I"><validators contentType="base64">HEweMSAyMTQ3NDgzNjQ3HQ==</validators><help>In a grid layout, a number of grid rows the component spans for. In an absolute layout, the height of the component in pixels.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Custom Classes" name="customClasses" type="S"><help>Custom CSS classes that may be used in the CSS style related properties.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Style" editor="code" name="style" type="S"><editorOptions>scss</editorOptions><help>The CSS Style to be applied to the component.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Visible Children" name="visibleChildren" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Wrapper Style" editor="code" name="containerStyle" type="S"><editorOptions>scss</editorOptions><help>CSS style to be applied to the component's wrapper.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Visible" name="preloaderVisible" type="B"><help>Toggles whether the preloader is displayed. When true, the entire component will be hidden behind the preloader during the loading phase.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Class Name" name="preloaderClass" type="S"><help>CSS class name to add to the preloader image and text.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Text" name="preloaderText" type="S"><help>Text to display in the preloader.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Icon" name="preloaderIcon" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Generate Mouse Clicked Events" name="generateMouseClicked" type="B"><help>Controls whether the component generated Mouse Clicked events. Initially disabled for performance reasons.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Generate Mouse Double Clicked Events" name="generateMouseDoubleClicked" type="B"><help>Controls whether the component generated Mouse Double events. Initially disabled for performance reasons.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Generate Mouse Pressed Events" name="generateMousePressed" type="B"><help>Controls whether the component generated Mouse Pressed events. Initially disabled for performance reasons.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Generate Mouse Released Events" name="generateMouseReleased" type="B"><help>Controls whether the component generated Mouse Released events. Initially disabled for performance reasons.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Generate Mouse Entered Events" name="generateMouseEntered" type="B"><help>Controls whether the component generated Mouse Entered events. Initially disabled for performance reasons.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Generate Mouse Exited Events" name="generateMouseExited" type="B"><help>Controls whether the component generated Mouse Exited events. Initially disabled for performance reasons.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Generate Key Pressed Events" name="generateKeyPressed" type="B"><help>Controls whether the component generated Key Pressed events. Initially disabled for performance reasons.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Generate Key Released Events" name="generateKeyReleased" type="B"><help>Controls whether the component generated Key Released events. Initially disabled for performance reasons.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Component Bindings" name="componentBindings" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Record Count" name="recordCount" type="I"><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Enable Kebab Menu" name="additionalActionEnable" type="B"><help>If enabled, adds a rightmost kebab menu column with configurable buttons to the data table.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Show Menu Items Inside Row" name="additionalActionShowInRow" type="B"><help>If enabled, additional action buttons are shown instead of a drop-down kebab menu. A separate button is shown instead of each kebab menu item.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Kebab Menu Icon" name="additionalActionIcon" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Kebab Menu Width" name="additionalActionWidth" type="I"><help>Width of the kebab menu icon (or action buttons, if Show Kebab Menu Items Inside Row is enabled) in pixels.</help><defaultValue>50</defaultValue></field><field description="additionalActionIconExtension" hidden="true" name="additionalActionIconExtension" type="S"><defaultValue/></field><field description="Kebab Menu Items" name="additionalActionSettings" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Kebab Menu Style" editor="code" name="additionalActionStyle" type="S"><editorOptions>scss</editorOptions><help>CSS style applied to kebab menu elements.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Enable Search" name="enableSearch" type="B"><help>Allows searching throughout the data in the component.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Search Placeholder" name="searchPlaceholder" type="S"><help>Message displayed in the search field when there is no user-entered text in it.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Data Table" name="dataTable" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Read Only" name="readOnly" type="B"><help>When enabled, the user is prevented from editing values in the data table.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Show Toolbar" name="showToolbar" type="B"><help>Controls whether the component's toolbar will be displayed.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Add Button Text" name="addButtonText" type="S"><help>Additional text to display next to the new row creation button.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Generate Row Added Events" name="generateRowAddedEvents" type="B"><help>Controls generation of Row Added events.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Generate Row Removed Events" name="generateRowRemovedEvents" type="B"><help>Controls generation of Row Removed events.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Generate Cell Updated Events" name="generateCellUpdatedEvents" type="B"><help>Controls generation of Cell Updated events.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Multiple Column Sorting" name="multipleSorting" type="B"><help>If enabled, allows sorting the data by more than one column.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Enable Context Menu" name="enableContextMenu" type="B"><help>Determines whether the context menu will be displayed when a right-click is performed on a cell of the data table.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Show Import Button" name="showImportButton" type="B"><help>Controls whether the import button will be displayed to the user.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Show Export Button" name="showExportButton" type="B"><help>Controls whether the export button will be displayed to the user.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Record ID Column Name" name="idColumn" type="S"><help>&lt;p>String that exactly matches one of the column names found in the Data Table property. When provided, the indicated column will be treated as the column containing the unique key for each row of the table. Each value in the indicated column must be unique for each row of the data table.&lt;/p>&lt;p>Note that in regular tables unique column values are enforced by declaring a field as a Key field in the table format and adding a Key Field validator. However, if a table is rendered in tree table mode, this property ensures that a record has a unique field value at each tree level.&lt;/p></help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Selected Rows Expression" editor="expression" name="selectedRowsExpression" type="S"><help>Expression to indicate which rows of the data table to display as selected. Expression is evaluated for every row of the data table, if the evaluation result is True, the row is displayed as selected, otherwise the row will be displayed as not selected. Expression is evaluated every time the data table is changed.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Has Selected Rows" name="hasSelectedRows" type="B"><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Column Settings" name="columnsSettings" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Maximum Height Without Vertical Scrolling" name="heightScrollEnabled" type="I"><help>Maximum height in pixels from which vertical scrolling is enabled in the data table's cells.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Items Per Page" extendableSelectionValues="true" name="pageSize" type="I"><validators contentType="base64">HFIeXi0xJHxeWzEtOV1cZCokHQ==</validators><selectionValues><option description="Auto">-1</option></selectionValues><help>Number of records to display on a single page.</help><defaultValue>-1</defaultValue></field><field description="Custom 'Items per Page' Selection Values" name="pageSizeOptions" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Show 'Items per Page' Selector" name="showPageSizeSelector" type="B"><help>Controls whether page size selector will be displayed, allowing users to choose a number of records shown on a page.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="'Items per Page' Selector Type" name="pageSizeSelectorType" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Combo Box">combobox</option><option description="Button Group">button-group</option></selectionValues><help>Type of the page size selector: a combo box or a group of buttons.</help><defaultValue>combobox</defaultValue></field><field description="currentPage" hidden="true" name="currentPage" type="I"><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Width table" name="widthTable" type="I"><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Enable Multiple Row Selection" name="checkRows" type="B"><help>If enabled, allows selecting rows using checkboxes.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Default Row Color" name="oddDefaultRowColor" nullable="true" type="C"><help>Background color to be applied to odd-numbered rows of the data table.</help><group>Odd Row</group><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Default Row Color" name="evenDefaultRowColor" nullable="true" type="C"><help>Background color to be applied to even-numbered rows of the data table.</help><group>Even Row</group><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Hover Row Color" name="oddHoverRowColor" nullable="true" type="C"><help>Background color to be applied to odd-numbered rows of the data table when they are hovered with the mouse.</help><group>Odd Row</group><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Hover Row Color" name="evenHoverRowColor" nullable="true" type="C"><help>Background color to be applied to even-numbered rows of the data table when they are hovered with the mouse.</help><group>Even Row</group><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Selected Row Color" name="oddSelectedRowColor" nullable="true" type="C"><help>Background color to be applied to odd-numbered rows of the data table when they are selected.</help><group>Odd Row</group><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Selected Row Color" name="evenSelectedRowColor" nullable="true" type="C"><help>Background color to be applied to even-numbered rows of the data table when they are selected.</help><group>Even Row</group><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Hover Selected Row Color" name="oddHoverSelectedRowColor" nullable="true" type="C"><help>Background color to be applied to odd-numbered rows of the data table when they are selected and hovered with the mouse.</help><group>Odd Row</group><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Hover Selected Row Color" name="evenHoverSelectedRowColor" nullable="true" type="C"><help>Background color to be applied to even-numbered rows of the data table when they are selected and hovered with the mouse.</help><group>Even Row</group><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Column Enabling Row Read-only Mode" name="columnToDefineRowLock" type="S"><help>Name of a Boolean-type column false values in that will make table rows read-only.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Column Enabling Kebab Menu" name="columnToDefineKebabLock" type="S"><help>Name of a Boolean-type column in the table. Kebab menu will be active only in rows where this column's value is True.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Column To Define Name For Nested Table" name="columnToDefineNameForNestedTable" type="S"><help>Name of a column that defines the name for the nested table.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Allow Column Resizing" name="resizableColumn" type="B"><help>Controls whether column resizing is enabled.</help><group>default</group><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Row Removal Confirmation" name="confirmActionDelete" type="B"><help>If enabled, the Delete Row action will require confirmation.</help><group>default</group><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Row Addition Confirmation" name="confirmActionAdd" type="B"><help>If enabled, the Add Row action will require confirmation.</help><group>default</group><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Fixed Format" name="fixedFormat" type="B"><help>If disabled, the Data Table property will accept data tables of any format. If enabled, the Data Table property will only accept data in the format specified by the Format property.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Format" name="format" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Filter Icon" name="filterIcon" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="filterIconExtension" hidden="true" name="filterIconExtension" type="S"><defaultValue/></field><field description="Search Icon" name="searchIcon" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="searchIconExtension" hidden="true" name="searchIconExtension" type="S"><defaultValue/></field><field description="Enable Column Visibility Control" name="enableColumnVisibility" type="B"><help>When enabled, displays a vertical kebab toolbar menu which displays a list of columns. User can check or uncheck columns from the list to show or hide columns.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Show Horizontal Fit Button" name="showHorizontalFitButton" type="B"><help>Controls whether the horizontal fit button will be displayed to the user.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Horizontal Fit" name="horizontalFit" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Auto">auto</option><option description="Enabled">enabled</option><option description="Disabled">disabled</option></selectionValues><help>Controls the horizontal fit mode.</help><defaultValue>auto</defaultValue></field><field description="Enable Advanced Search" name="enableAdvancedSearch" type="B"><help>Enables advanced searching and filtering options for the component.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Smart Filter Expression" name="smartFilterExpression" type="S"><defaultValue/></field><field description="Smart Filter Display Mode" name="smartFilterDisplayMode" type="S"><defaultValue>SMART_FILTER_COMPONENT_MODE</defaultValue></field><field description="Smart Filter Control States" name="smartFilterControlStates" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Manually Configure Column Width" name="manualConfigureColumnWidth" type="B"><help>&lt;p>When enabled, the table will use the Width defined in the Column Settings property for each column. This can significantly improve performance, particularly for large tables, by reducing the time required to automatically calculate and adjust column widths.&lt;/p>&lt;p>A Width must be defined in the Column Settings property for every column in the table when enabling this property.&lt;/p></help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Original Format" name="originalFormat" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Scale" name="printScale" type="I"><defaultValue>100</defaultValue></field></fields></format></entry><entry><int>30</int><format maxRecords="1" minRecords="1"><fields><field description="Parent Record ID Column Name" name="parentIdColumnName" type="S"><help>Name of a column that contains unique IDs of the parent records. This column should have Null values for top-level records that don't have parents.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Indent Size" name="indentSize" type="I"><help>Indent size for each level of nesting, in pixels.</help><defaultValue>15</defaultValue></field><field description="Visible Children" name="visibleChildren" type="I"><help>Number of visible children.</help><defaultValue>10</defaultValue></field></fields></format></entry><entry><int>31</int><format><fields><field description="Record ID" keyfield="true" name="recordId" type="S"><help>Unique ID of an initially expanded record.</help><defaultValue/></field></fields></format></entry><entry><int>32</int><format><fields><field description="Unique Column" extendableSelectionValues="true" keyfield="true" name="uniqueColumn" type="S"><help>Unique column.</help><defaultValue/></field></fields></format></entry><entry><int>33</int><format><fields><field description="UID" name="uid" type="S"><help>Item's unique ID.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Description" name="desc" type="S"><help>Item description.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Icon" name="icon" type="A"><help>Image of the item in regular state.</help><defaultValue><data><nullValue/></data></defaultValue></field><field description="Hover Icon" name="iconHover" type="A"><help>Image of the item in mouse-hovered state.</help><defaultValue><data><nullValue/></data></defaultValue></field><field description="Active Icon" name="iconActive" type="A"><help>Image of the item in active (clicked) state.</help><defaultValue><data><nullValue/></data></defaultValue></field><field description="Action" name="buttonAction" type="S"><selectionValues><option description=""/><option description="Edit">edit</option><option description="Delete">delete</option><option description="Cancel">cancel</option><option description="Apply">apply</option></selectionValues><help>&lt;p>Action to be executed for the corresponding row by selecting the menu item or pressing the action button:&lt;/p>&lt;ul>&lt;li>&lt;strong>Edit&lt;/strong>. Starts editing current row.&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;strong>Delete&lt;/strong>. Deletes current row.&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;strong>Cancel&lt;/strong>. Cancels editing of current row and discards changes.&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;strong>Apply&lt;/strong>. Stops editing of current row and applies changes.&lt;/li>&lt;/ul></help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Confirmation" name="confirm" type="B"><help>If enabled, all kebab menu actions will require confirmation.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Confirmation Message" name="confirmTitle" type="S"><help>Text of the confirmation message.</help><defaultValue/></field></fields></format></entry><entry><int>34</int><format maxRecords="0"/></entry><entry><int>35</int><format><fields><field description="Name" name="name" type="S"><help>Name of the column to apply settings for.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Fixed Column" name="fixed" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Left">left</option><option description="Right">right</option><option description="Unset">unset</option></selectionValues><help>If not Unset, allows fixing the column on the Left or Right side of the table, effectively changing the column's position. A fixed column ignores horizontal scrolling.</help><defaultValue>unset</defaultValue></field><field description="Header Text Behavior" name="headerTextBehavior" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Expand Column">expandColumn</option><option description="Ellipsis">ellipsis</option><option description="Word Wrap">wordWrap</option></selectionValues><help>&lt;p>Controls how the column header is displayed if a header text does not fit into the default column width:&lt;/p>&lt;ul>&lt;li>Expand Column allows the column width to expand enough to accommodate the header text in a single line.&lt;/li>&lt;li>Ellipsis truncates header text&lt;/li>&lt;li>Word Wrap maintains column width by expanding column height and displaying header text on multiple lines. Columns with no text and no content will be displayed with a certain minimum column width.&lt;/li>&lt;/ul></help><defaultValue>expandColumn</defaultValue></field><field description="Word Break" name="wordBreak" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Break All">break-all</option><option description="Break Word">break-word</option><option description="Don't Break">false</option></selectionValues><help>&lt;p>Defines line breaks mode for the column's regular cells:&lt;/p>&lt;ul>&lt;li>Break All allows breaking text at any character&lt;/li>&lt;li>Break Word allows breaking at the end of any word&lt;/li>&lt;li>Don't Break completely prohibits breaking text into several lines&lt;/li>&lt;/ul></help><defaultValue>false</defaultValue></field><field description="Visible Length" name="visibleLength" nullable="true" type="I"><help>Maximum number of characters of a string to display in the renderer. The full value will be displayed in the mouse-over tooltip.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Cell Text Horizontal Alignment" name="textAlignHorizontal" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Center">center</option><option description="Left">left</option><option description="Right">right</option></selectionValues><help>Horizontal position of the text in the column cell.</help><defaultValue>center</defaultValue></field><field description="Header Text Horizontal Alignment" name="textAlignHeaderHorizontal" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Center">center</option><option description="Left">left</option><option description="Right">right</option></selectionValues><help>Horizontal position of the text in the column header.</help><defaultValue>center</defaultValue></field><field description="Cell Text Vertical Alignment" name="textAlignVertical" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Bottom">bottom </option><option description="Middle">middle</option><option description="Top">top</option></selectionValues><help>Vertical position of the text in the column cell.</help><defaultValue>middle</defaultValue></field><field description="Header Text Vertical Alignment" name="textAlignHeaderVertical" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Bottom">bottom </option><option description="Middle">middle</option><option description="Top">top</option></selectionValues><help>Vertical position of the text in the column header.</help><defaultValue>middle</defaultValue></field><field description="Sorter" name="sorter" type="B"><help>Enables sorting by the column.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Sorter Preset" name="sorterPreset" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Ascending">ASC</option><option description="Descending">DESC</option><option description="Unset">unset</option></selectionValues><help>If not Unset, defines the default sort order for the column.</help><defaultValue>unset</defaultValue></field><field description="Filtering" extendableSelectionValues="true" name="filtering" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="None">none</option><option description="Match String">matchString</option><option description="Filter">filter</option></selectionValues><help>Enables searching and filtering by column data.</help><defaultValue>none</defaultValue></field><field description="Filter Table" name="filterTable" type="T"><help>&lt;p>Custom search criteria for the column if Search is enabled for it:&lt;/p>&lt;ul>&lt;li>&lt;b>Value&lt;/b> means that searching and filtering work by string representations of raw cell values&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Description&lt;/b> means that searching and filtering work by human-readable selection value descriptions rather than raw cell values&lt;/li>&lt;/ul></help><defaultValue><table><format><fields><field description="Value" name="value" type="S"><defaultValue/></field><field description="Description" name="text" type="S"><defaultValue/></field><field description="Checked" name="checked" type="B"><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field></fields></format></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Match String" name="matchString" type="S"><help>Match string.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Width" name="width" type="I"><help>Column width, in pixels.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Visible" name="visibility" type="B"><help>Controls whether the column should be displayed to the user.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Index" name="index" type="I"><help>Controls the initial order of the columns, with 0 being the leftmost column.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Loading" name="loading" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Eager">eager</option><option description="Lazy">lazy</option></selectionValues><help>Provides a hint to the browser on how to handle the loading of the image which is currently outside the window's visual viewport. This helps to optimize the loading of the document's contents by postponing loading the image until it's expected to be needed, rather than immediately during the initial page load.</help><defaultValue>eager</defaultValue></field></fields></format></entry><entry><int>36</int><format><fields><field description="Column" name="COMPONENT_SMART_FILTER_COLUMN" type="S"><defaultValue/></field><field description="Filter Type" name="COMPONENT_SMART_FILTER_TYPE" type="I"><selectionValues><option description="Undefined">0</option><option description="Numeric">1</option><option description="String">2</option><option description="Boolean">3</option><option description="Color">4</option><option description="Date">5</option><option description="Table">6</option><option description="Data Block">7</option></selectionValues><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Filter State" name="COMPONENT_SMART_FILTER_STATE" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field></fields></format></entry><entry><int>37</int><format maxRecords="1" minRecords="1"><fields><field description="Original Format" name="originalFormat" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Original Format Compatibility" name="originalFormatCompatibility" type="B"><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field></fields></format></entry><entry><int>38</int><format maxRecords="1" minRecords="1"><fields><field description="Name" name="name" nullable="true" type="S"><validators contentType="base64">HFIeXHcrXl5OYW1lIG1heSBjb250YWluIG9ubHkgTGF0aW4gbGV0dGVycywgZGlnaXRzLCBhbmQgdW5kZXJzY29yZXMd</validators><help>Unique name of the UI component within the dashboard. Since all UI components are represented by contexts located in the two-level component context tree, a component's name also equals to both the name and full path of the component context.</help><defaultValue>STUB</defaultValue></field><field description="Content Overflow" name="overflow" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Auto">auto</option><option description="Hidden">hidden</option><option description="Scroll">scroll</option><option description="Unset">unset</option><option description="Visible">visible</option></selectionValues><help>&lt;p>Behavior of the content if it overflows the container:&lt;/p>&lt;ul>&lt;li>&lt;b>Auto&lt;/b> — scrollbar will be enabled automatically once the content overflows the container&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Hidden&lt;/b> — all overflowed content will be hidden&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Scroll&lt;/b> — scrollbar is always enabled even if content doesn't overflow the container&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Unset&lt;/b> — cancels inheritance of this property from any sources (e.g. dashboard Style property)&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Visible&lt;/b> — the content will always be visible even it overflows the container&lt;/li>&lt;/ul></help><defaultValue>auto</defaultValue></field><field description="Visible" name="visible" type="B"><help>Controls whether the component is displayed.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Variables Storage" name="variablesStorage" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Breakpoint Data" name="gridBreakpoints" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Context Menu" name="contextMenu" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Show Header" name="showHeader" type="B"><help>Configures whether 