tValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Show Time" name="timeDisplayed" type="B"><help>Allows a user to choose a time as well as a date.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Range Buttons" name="rangeButtons" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Default Start Date" editor="date" name="startDate" nullable="true" type="D"><help>Selected date/time in case if the Date Range property is disabled. Start date/time of a time range in case if the Date Range property is enabled.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Default End Date" editor="date" name="endDate" nullable="true" type="D"><help>End date/time of a time range.</help><defaultValue><nullValue/></defaultValue></field><field description="Disabled" name="disabled" type="B"><help>Enables or disables the component. Disabled components don't respond to user input and are rendered as grayed-out.</help><group>default</group><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Dropdown Style" editor="code" name="dropdownStyle" nullable="true" type="S"><editorOptions>scss</editorOptions><help>Style for the popup picker.</help><defaultValue/></field></fields></format></entry><entry><int>40</int><format><fields><field description="Name" name="name" type="S"><help>Text of the button label.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Date Range" name="range" type="I"><help>Number of time units to select.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Direction" name="direction" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Back">back</option><option description="Forward">forward</option><option description="Today">today</option></selectionValues><help>&lt;p>Direction of the date selection:&lt;/p>&lt;ul>&lt;li>&lt;strong>Forward&lt;/strong> — selects the number of units after the current date&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;strong>Today&lt;/strong> — selects the current day, so Range, Step, and Dynamic Step properties will be ignored&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;strong>Back&lt;/strong> — selects the number of units before the current date&lt;/li>&lt;/ul></help><defaultValue>forward</defaultValue></field><field description="Step" name="step" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Hour">hour</option><option description="Month">month</option><option description="Day">day</option></selectionValues><help>Time unit to use for selection.</help><defaultValue>day</defaultValue></field><field description="Dynamic Step" name="dynamicStep" type="B"><help>Allows the defined range to be shifted by the value specified in the Range property each time the button is pressed.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field></fields></format></entry><entry><int>41</int><format maxRecords="1" minRecords="1"><fields><field description="Name" name="name" nullable="true" type="S"><validators contentType="base64">HFIeXHcrXl5OYW1lIG1heSBjb250YWluIG9ubHkgTGF0aW4gbGV0dGVycywgZGlnaXRzLCBhbmQgdW5kZXJzY29yZXMd</validators><help>Unique name of the UI component within the dashboard. Since all UI components are represented by contexts located in the two-level component context tree, a component's name also equals to both the name and full path of the component context.</help><defaultValue>STUB</defaultValue></field><field description="Content Overflow" name="overflow" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Auto">auto</option><option description="Hidden">hidden</option><option description="Scroll">scroll</option><option description="Unset">unset</option><option description="Visible">visible</option></selectionValues><help>&lt;p>Behavior of the content if it overflows the container:&lt;/p>&lt;ul>&lt;li>&lt;b>Auto&lt;/b> — scrollbar will be enabled automatically once the content overflows the container&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Hidden&lt;/b> — all overflowed content will be hidden&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Scroll&lt;/b> — scrollbar is always enabled even if content doesn't overflow the container&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Unset&lt;/b> — cancels inheritance of this property from any sources (e.g. dashboard Style property)&lt;/li>&lt;li>&lt;b>Visible&lt;/b> — the content will always be visible even it overflows the container&lt;/li>&lt;/ul></help><defaultValue>auto</defaultValue></field><field description="Visible" name="visible" type="B"><help>Controls whether the component is displayed.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Variables Storage" name="variablesStorage" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Breakpoint Data" name="gridBreakpoints" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Context Menu" name="contextMenu" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Show Header" name="showHeader" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window header should be displayed.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Header Title" name="dockTitle" type="S"><help>Dockable window header text.</help><aliases><alias>description</alias></aliases><defaultValue/></field><field description="Header Icon" name="dockIcon" type="T"><defaultValue><table><format/></table></defaultValue></field><field description="Maximizable" name="maximizable" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window can be maximized.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Collapsible" name="collapsible" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window can be collapsed.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Movable" name="dockMovable" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window can be moved.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Collapsed" name="dockCollapsed" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window is collapsed.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Floatable" name="dockFloatable" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window can be floated.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Resizable" name="dockResizable" type="B"><help>Configures whether the dockable window can be resized.</help><defaultValue>1</defaultValue></field><field description="Tab Position" name="dockTabPosition" type="S"><selectionValues><option description="Top">top</option><option description="Bottom">bottom</option><option description="Left">left</option><option description="Right">right</option></selectionValues><help>Configures the position of tabs appearing when the dockable window is stacked into a tabbed panel with other windows.</help><defaultValue>top</defaultValue></field><field description="Preferred Width" name="dockPreferredWidth" type="I"><help>Desired width of the dockable window when split into another component or a dashboard.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Preferred Height" name="dockPreferredHeight" type="I"><help>Desired height of the dockable window when split into another component or a dashboard.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Minimum Width" name="dockMinimumWidth" type="I"><help>Minimum width of the dockable window when split into another component or a dashboard. Overridden when the viewscreen does not have sufficient space for the minimum width.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Minimum Height" name="dockMinimumHeight" type="I"><help>Minimum height of the dockable window when split into another component or a dashboard. Overridden when the viewscreen does not have sufficient space for the minimum height.</help><defaultValue>0</defaultValue></field><field description="Tab ID" name="tabId" type="S"><help>Dockable tab identifier, which by default is the dockable component name.</help><defaultValue/></field><field description="Panel ID" name="panelId" type="S"><help>Identified of the panel the dockable component is located in.</h